# Manual iPhone report round two — legibility of chart/bill/history surfaces (bug batch 4, P1–P7)
All seven verified by tests/e2e/run.mjs ("ui-polish" sections) in Edge at a 390×844 phone viewport; test-results/e2e-run.txt holds the PASS lines. Ledger: tasks/bugs-4.md (ids P1–P7). Unlike the Z-batch tap-zoom claims these read computed styles/geometry, so a regression goes RED on the desktop instead of hiding on Safari.
Evidence: pre-fix pass printed 15 FAIL rows for P1…P7 with the rest of the pass green; post-fix pass → ALL 182 acceptance checks GREEN, exit 0, no [wait-timeout], [elapsed] 12.1s; unit gate → OK unit layer — 14/14 exports exercised.

- [x] Given a chart card: Then its name+unit header is a full-width line ABOVE every bar (column flow), not a caption squeezed beside the bars at the left edge. (`P1`)
- [x] Given bars: Then nothing paints inside the coloured pill — each month gets an axis caption under its bar and the month→value pairs read as one horizontal legend line for the card (a key to the bars, not micro-text in the paint). (`P2`)
- [x] Given a Bills meter row with readings typed: Then its Δ/calculation preview paints as plain text — no HTML strikethrough across the numbers (that is what "the final calculations string looks dashed" was). (`P3`)
- [x] Given any Bills meter row (price untouched at its default): Then the per-unit line STATES the price actually used, formatted `{number} ₽ per {unit}` from an STR template, and stays visible — no more bare "₽ per unit" caption hiding a figure. (`P4`, plus a unit case for the new STR key)
- [x] Given the Bills and Settings cards: Then meter/config rows and the add-new-meter block are flat blocks on one card (transparent fill, no inner shadow), so the page stops reading as a card nested inside a card while keeping its rhythm and widths. (`P5`)
- [x] Given the History tab: Then the CSV-save button hugs its own copy instead of being stretched across the whole phone width, and stays a comfortable tap target (as do Apply/Clear on Settings). (`P6`)
- [x] Given saved months in History: Then each month is a small section — a heading line with the total plus a four-column table (meter name | reading | Δ reading | ₽ per unit) with one row per meter — not one run-on sentence; its raw total stays machine-readable for the money-agreement claim. (`P7`, plus a unit case that the descriptor carries that month's own reading and price)
